\DOC DISCARD_NONMATCHING_ASSUMPTIONS

\TYPE {DISCARD_NONMATCHING_ASSUMPTIONS : term list -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Discards every assumption that fails to match any of the supplied term
patterns, leaving the conclusion unchanged.

\DESCRIBE
The argument {pats : term list} is a list of term patterns: an assumption
survives only if it matches one of them, and all others are dropped. The
surviving assumptions keep their relative order in the assumption list.
{
        A ?- t
     ====================  DISCARD_NONMATCHING_ASSUMPTIONS pats
        A' ?- t
}
\noindent where {A'} is the sublist of {A} consisting of those assumptions
matching some pattern in {pats}.

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces, the tactic only performs this filtering, always
yielding a single subgoal, and is applied only to goals whose assumptions are
machine-state facts, with the same pattern list supplied throughout; the number
of assumptions removed ranges from one to most of them.

\ENDDOC
